# tests/fixtures/upstream-manifests/ubuntu-base-24.04.4-base-amd64.packages
# — the installed-package inventory of the ubuntu-base tarball itself
# (GitHub issue #140; SPEC.md §12 R11, §11 M7).
#
# WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS: tests/unit/210-upstream-manifest-parity.sh used
# to diff ubuntnix's declared, locked closure (archive.lock.json) directly
# against Canonical's upstream Server manifest and report the difference as
# "missing from ubuntnix." That is wrong for a composed ubuntnix system:
# nix/compose.nix's composeRootfs (see its header, and the "ubuntu-base
# plus every declared package" line at nix/compose.nix:95/291) builds every
# rootfs as the ubuntu-base tarball UNPACKED FIRST, with the locked closure
# layered on top. A package that ships inside ubuntu-base itself — bash,
# dash, grep, gzip, util-linux, base-files, login, and so on — is present
# on every real composed system whether or not archive.lock.json also lists
# it. Treating those as "missing" overstated the R11 gap. This fixture lets
# 210 compute the honest effective package set (base ∪ closure) instead of
# closure alone, without needing to fetch or unpack the 30MB tarball in CI.
#
# PROVENANCE
#   Source tarball: ubuntu-base-24.04.4-base-amd64.tar.gz
#   Source URL:     https://cdimage.ubuntu.com/ubuntu-base/releases/24.04/release/ubuntu-base-24.04.4-base-amd64.tar.gz
#   Tarball SHA-256: c1e67ef7b17a6300e136118bd1dc04725009cb376c1aad10abcf8cd453628d58
#     (this is the exact same digest nix/stdenv.nix pins at its `sha256`
#     assignment for `tarball` — see that file's own "Trust root" comment
#     for how it was independently reproduced. tests/unit/213-ubuntu-base-
#     fixture-pin.sh parses nix/stdenv.nix's pin at test time and fails if
#     it and the value recorded here ever disagree, so this fixture cannot
#     silently drift onto a different ubuntu-base spin than the one the
#     build actually fetches.)
#   Derivation:     the tarball was downloaded, its SHA-256 independently
#     verified against the digest above, then extracted; this file lists
#     every package name whose entry in the extracted tree's own
#     var/lib/dpkg/status has a `Status:` field ending in `installed`
#     (dpkg's own definition of "actually installed," as opposed to a
#     stale/half-configured/removed-but-not-purged entry) — i.e. exactly
#     the package set dpkg itself considers present on a freshly-unpacked
#     ubuntu-base rootfs, before any of ubuntnix's own composeRootfs step
#     layers the locked closure on top.
#   Derived:        2026-08-12
#   Count:          91 package names, sorted, one per line, no duplicates.
#
# Format: one binary package name per line (no version, no `:arch` suffix
# — ubuntu-base is single-arch amd64 so no multiarch suffix ever appears).
# Regenerate with, from an independently-verified copy of the tarball:
#   tar xzf ubuntu-base-24.04.4-base-amd64.tar.gz -O var/lib/dpkg/status \
#     | awk '/^Package: /{p=$2} /^Status: .* installed$/{print p}' \
#     | sort -u
